<BaseLayout title="About Kuoo" description="Who maintains Kuoo, how its AI tool, harness and local-model guides are prepared, and how to check sources, understand evidence limits and report corrections." lang="en">
  <article class="card">
    <h1>About Kuoo</h1>
    <p>Kuoo is an independently maintained, bilingual site for developers and small teams using AI tools and models. Its topics include coding agents and harnesses, local-model deployment, automation and engineering methods. Existing OpenClaw guides remain available. The site is not affiliated with the products discussed here.</p>
    <h2>Who maintains the site</h2>
    <p>The website source and its change history are published in <a href="https://github.com/duoglas/openclaw-hub" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">duoglas/openclaw-hub</a>. The repository maintainer is the contact for site content and corrections.</p>
    <h2>How to use the content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Some articles and briefs are prepared with AI assistance and automated publishing workflows. That does not mean every claim or command has been independently tested.</li>
      <li>Read the publication date and linked sources. Product versions, prices, availability, and commands can change after publication.</li>
      <li>Back up your configuration before following a technical guide. Check the current official documentation before using a command in production.</li>
      <li>News briefs summarize sources; they are not original reporting. Follow the source links for the full context.</li>
      <li>New evidence-reviewed guides distinguish documentation analysis from hands-on tests. Source checks, model reviews and actual runtime tests are separate steps; read the stated limits.</li>
      <li>Private notes may inform research questions, but private conversations and unapproved personal cases are not publication sources. Published claims require public sources or explicitly publishable test evidence.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Corrections and commercial links</h2>
    <p>If a step fails or a source is wrong, please <a href="/en/contact/">report the page and the specific issue</a>. A report is not a promise of a response time or of technical support.</p>
    <p>The site includes Google AdSense code and some affiliate links. A qualifying purchase through an affiliate link may earn the site a commission. Neither an advertisement nor a commercial link is a guarantee of a product's suitability.</p>
    <p>See <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy &amp; ads</a> for information about third-party services.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
